# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-avc/openavc-drivers/main/avcdriver.schema.json
#
# Sennheiser SpeechLine CHG 2N / CHG 4N network chargers
#
# Controls the CHG 2N (two bays) and CHG 4N (four bays) over Sennheiser Sound
# Control (SSC) version 1: JSON objects over UDP port 45, one object per
# datagram.
#
# Protocol reference: "Sennheiser Sound Control Protocol (SSC) - Developer's
# guide for SpeechLine Digital Wireless", TI 1094 v4.3, chapters 4-6 and
# 13-15 (CHG 2N / CHG 4N firmware 3.0.0); source_url below.
#
# Wire format (§4): every address is a path of JSON keys. A null argument
# reads it ({"bays":{"charging":null}}), any other value writes it, and the
# reply carries the value now in force. A refusal is
# {"osc":{"error":[{"bays":{"serial":[406]}}]}} (§14.4, §15).
#
# The bays. Every bay value is one array with an element per bay, in bay
# order: {"bays":{"bat_gauge":[0,100,64,30]}} (§14.42-14.54). Each bay is a
# child here, and each element is read into its bay by position. An empty
# bay reports false, 0 or "" in its element.
#
# Push, not polling (§5): the charger notifies a subscribed client of every
# change on the socket the subscription came from. A subscription lasts the
# lifetime the client asks for (10 s by default, §14.11) and at most 1000
# notifications, then ends with error 310 (§5.1); sending the same request
# again renews it. Every subscribable address is subscribed with a lifetime of
# 90 s and the poll renews them all (the Poll Interval stops at 30 s, so every
# lifetime spans three renewals). A 310 subscribes everything again at once.
# The charger answers every subscription with the current value, so the
# renewal is also a full resync. Each bay's transmitter type and error state
# cannot be subscribed (§14.43, §14.54), so they are read on every poll and
# again whenever the docked bays change (then_query, platform 0.38.0).
#
# One address per message. The document's only replies that repeat a name at
# one level answer a message that asked for several addresses or methods at
# once: an /osc/xid sent beside the subscription (§14.11 example 1). A JSON
# reader keeps the last of a repeated name, so OpenAVC 0.38.0 would lose the
# rest of such a reply. This driver sends one address in each message, reads
# and subscriptions alike, so nothing in the document repeats; from the
# release after 0.38.0 a repeated name is read under every copy anyway.
#
# Identify (§14.53) takes an array as long as the charger has bays. A command
# sends one template, so the Identify Bay picker is a list the driver
# publishes from the product name the charger reports (Identify Options):
# each choice is that model's own array.
#
# Liveness: the method list has no /osc/ping, so the probe asks the product
# name, a fixed question every unit answers; any reply counts, an error
# included.
#
# Format: YAML. Every address is a fixed JSON string, every value a json: true
# rule, each bay a literal child id, and the subscriptions are queries like
# any other.
#
# NOT hardware-verified. Built from the document and its own examples.

id: sennheiser_sl_chg
name: Sennheiser SpeechLine CHG 2N / CHG 4N Charger
manufacturer: Sennheiser
category: audio
version: "1.0.1"
author: OpenAVC
min_platform_version: "0.37.0"
description: >
  Monitors the Sennheiser SpeechLine CHG 2N and CHG 4N network chargers over
  Sennheiser Sound Control (JSON over UDP, port 45). For every bay: whether a
  transmitter is docked, its type, serial number and firmware, whether it is
  charging, its charge, time to full, battery bars, health and cycles, and the
  bay's error state (communication, update, overcurrent, charging voltage).
  Identify a bay, names, restart and factory reset. State is push-driven: the
  driver subscribes and the charger reports every change as it happens.

source_url: https://assets.sennheiser.com/download/assets/TI_1094_v4.3_Sennheiser_Sound_Control_Protocol_SL_DW_EN.pdf/b2a3c92ce7bb11f088db768ee8e97aea
tags: [wireless, microphone, charger, speechline, battery, ssc]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [sennheiser_ssc]
ports: [45]

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Sennheiser
    models: [CHG 2N, CHG 4N]
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Built from Sennheiser's SSC developer guide for charger firmware 3.0.0;
      not yet run against a charger. The SL MCR 2 / 4 DW and SL Rack Receiver
      DW receivers use different SSC commands and have their own drivers.
      Network address configuration and firmware updates belong to Sennheiser
      Control Cockpit.

transport: udp

help:
  overview: >
    Shows each bay of a Sennheiser SpeechLine CHG 2N or CHG 4N charger: whether
    a transmitter is docked, its type and serial number, whether it is
    charging, its charge and time to full, its battery health and cycles, and
    any fault the bay reports. Everything that changes on the charger shows up
    here as it happens. Identify Bay flashes a bay's LEDs so it can be found.
  setup: >
    1. Give the charger a static IP address or a DHCP reservation, and note
       it.
    2. Enter that address here. Control uses UDP port 45; leave the port
       alone.
    3. Choose the number of bays: 2 for a CHG 2N, 4 for a CHG 4N. Once
       connected, the charger's model sets it, and it is saved here.
    4. The charger and the OpenAVC server must be able to exchange UDP traffic
       on port 45 in both directions. If the charger shows offline while
       Control Cockpit still sees it, check for a firewall between the two.
  connection: >
    The charger answers on UDP port 45. If Control Cockpit sees it and OpenAVC
    does not, a firewall between the server and the charger is blocking UDP 45.

discovery:
  # The chargers report "CHG2N" or "CHG4N" (§14.18); the SpeechLine receivers
  # report "SLDW" and "SLDW" with a channel count. Every SSC device answers
  # UDP 45, so the port alone proves nothing.
  udp_probe:
    port: 45
    send_ascii: '{"device":{"identity":{"product":null}}}'
    expect_regex: '"product"\s*:\s*"CHG[24]N"'
    timeout_ms: 1500
    extract:
      model:
        regex: '"product"\s*:\s*"(CHG[24]N)"'
        group: 1
    extract_manufacturer: "Sennheiser"
  oui:
    - "00:1b:66"   # Sennheiser electronic GmbH & Co. KG
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "sennheiser"

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 45
  bay_count: 4
  poll_interval: 30
  # The document states no minimum gap between messages; this is the
  # platform's default. Connect sends about thirty messages, one address each.
  inter_command_delay: 0.05

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: IP Address
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 45
    label: UDP Port
    help: "Sennheiser Sound Control listens on UDP port 45."
  bay_count:
    type: enum
    values: [2, 4]
    default: 4
    label: Charging Bays
    learned_from: bay_count_reported
    help: >
      2 for a CHG 2N, 4 for a CHG 4N. Once connected, the charger's model sets
      the bay count, and it is saved here.
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 30
    min: 5
    # Each subscription lives 90 s; at 30 s or less every one is renewed at
    # least twice before it would end.
    max: 30
    label: Poll Interval (sec)
    help: >
      How often the subscriptions are renewed, which also re-reads every
      value. The charger reports changes as they happen, so 30 s is plenty.
  inter_command_delay:
    type: number
    default: 0.05
    min: 0
    label: Inter-Command Delay (sec)
    help: "Pause between messages sent to the charger."

liveness:
  send: '{"device":{"identity":{"product":null}}}'
  # Any answer proves the charger is there, a refusal included.
  expect: '"product"|"error"'
  interval: 20
  timeout: 5
  max_failures: 2

# Reads first (none of these can be subscribed), then one subscription per
# address. Each subscription is written once here, with an anchor; the poll
# and the rules that subscribe again below reuse the same entries.
on_connect:
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"product":null}}}'
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"version":null}}}'
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"serial":null}}}'
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"vendor":null}}}'
  - '{"interface":{"version":null}}'
  - '{"device":{"network":{"ether":{"macs":null}}}}'
  - '{"device":{"network":{"ipv4":{"ipaddr":null}}}}'
  # ── The charger ──
  - &sub_name { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"name":null}}]}}}', query_for: device_name }
  - &sub_group { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"group":null}}]}}}', query_for: group }
  - &sub_location { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"location":null}}]}}}', query_for: location }
  - &sub_mdns { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"network":{"mdns_responder":null}}}]}}}', query_for: mdns_enabled }
  - &sub_state { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"state":null}}]}}}', query_for: device_state }
  - &sub_progress { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"progress":null}}]}}}', query_for: progress }
  - &sub_sl_image { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"ptxversion_sl":null}}]}}}', query_for: sl_firmware_image }
  - &sub_d1_image { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"device":{"ptxversion_d1":null}}]}}}', query_for: d1_firmware_image }
  # ── The bays (each answer is an array, one element per bay) ──
  - &sub_active { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"active":null}}]}}}', query_for: transmitters_docked }
  # Not subscribable: read after the docked bays are known.
  - &read_types '{"bays":{"device_type":null}}'
  - &read_bay_state '{"bays":{"state":null}}'
  # Pre-condition: a transmitter in one of the bays (§14.44).
  - &sub_serial { send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"serial":null}}]}}}', when_state: { transmitters_docked: true } }
  - &sub_version '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"version":null}}]}}}'
  - &sub_charging '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"charging":null}}]}}}'
  - &sub_gauge '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"bat_gauge":null}}]}}}'
  - &sub_timetofull '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"bat_timetofull":null}}]}}}'
  - &sub_bars '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"bat_bars":null}}]}}}'
  - &sub_health '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"bat_health":null}}]}}}'
  - &sub_cycles '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"bat_cycles":null}}]}}}'
  - &sub_identify '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"lifetime":90},"bays":{"identify":null}}]}}}'

# Renew every subscription each cycle: a renewal is the same request as the
# first one (§5.1) and its answer carries the current value. The two reads
# are here too, for the releases without then_query.
polling:
  queries:
    - *sub_name
    - *sub_group
    - *sub_location
    - *sub_mdns
    - *sub_state
    - *sub_progress
    - *sub_sl_image
    - *sub_d1_image
    - *sub_active
    - *read_types
    - *read_bay_state
    - *sub_serial
    - *sub_version
    - *sub_charging
    - *sub_gauge
    - *sub_timetofull
    - *sub_bars
    - *sub_health
    - *sub_cycles
    - *sub_identify

state_variables:
  # ── Identity and network ──
  model:
    type: string
    label: Model
    help: "The charger's product name: CHG2N or CHG4N."
  bay_count_reported:
    type: integer
    label: Bays
    help: "The number of charging bays, from the model."
  firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: Firmware Version
  serial_number:
    type: string
    label: Serial Number
  vendor:
    type: string
    label: Vendor
  interface_version:
    type: string
    label: SSC Interface Version
  mac_address:
    type: string
    label: MAC Address
  ip_address:
    type: string
    label: IP Address
  mdns_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: mDNS
    help: "The charger announces itself for discovery (takes effect after a restart)."
  # ── Names ──
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: Device Name
    help: "The charger's name, as shown in Control Cockpit and in device discovery."
  group:
    type: string
    label: Group
    help: "The charger's group name: up to 8 letters, digits, - and _."
  location:
    type: string
    label: Location
  # ── Charger ──
  device_state:
    type: enum
    values: [normal, firmware_update]
    label: Charger State
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "normal, or firmware_update while the charger updates its own firmware (it restarts at the end)."
  progress:
    type: integer
    label: Update Progress
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
    help: "How far the charger's firmware update has got."
  sl_firmware_image:
    type: string
    label: Stored SpeechLine Transmitter Firmware
    help: "The version of the SpeechLine transmitter firmware the charger holds for updating docked transmitters."
  d1_firmware_image:
    type: string
    label: Stored EW-D1 Transmitter Firmware
    help: "The version of the evolution wireless D1 transmitter firmware the charger holds for updating docked transmitters."
  transmitters_docked:
    type: boolean
    label: Transmitters Docked
    help: "At least one bay holds a transmitter."
  identify_options:
    type: string
    label: Identify Options
    help: "The choices Identify Bay offers for this model, set when the charger reports it."
  # ── Errors ──
  last_error:
    type: string
    label: Last Error
    help: "What the charger said about the last request it did not accept."
  last_error_code:
    type: integer
    label: Last Error Code

child_entity_types:
  bay:
    label: Bay
    label_plural: Bays
    id_format:
      type: integer
      min: 1
      max: 4
    instances:
      # The model sets the count (CHG 2N 2, CHG 4N 4); the config field is the
      # count before the charger has reported.
      count_from_state: bay_count_reported
      count_from: bay_count
      label: "Bay {id}"
    summary_fields: [docked, tx_type, tx_battery_percent, tx_charge_minutes, tx_charging, status]
    state_variables:
      docked:
        type: boolean
        label: Transmitter Docked
        cloud_priority: high
        help: "A transmitter is in this bay."
      tx_type:
        type: enum
        values: [handheld, bodypack]
        label: Transmitter Type
        help: "The docked transmitter's type; empty when the bay is empty."
      tx_serial:
        type: string
        label: Transmitter Serial Number
        help: "The docked transmitter's serial number; empty when the bay is empty."
      tx_firmware:
        type: string
        label: Transmitter Firmware
        help: "The docked transmitter's firmware version; empty when the bay is empty."
      tx_charging:
        type: boolean
        label: Charging
        cloud_priority: high
        help: "The docked transmitter is charging. False when the bay is empty or the battery is full."
      tx_battery_percent:
        type: integer
        label: Battery Charge
        min: 0
        max: 100
        unit: "%"
        cloud_priority: high
        help: "Charge in the docked transmitter's battery; 0 when the bay is empty."
      tx_charge_minutes:
        type: integer
        label: Time to Full Charge
        unit: min
        help: "Minutes until the docked transmitter is fully charged; 0 when it is full or the bay is empty."
      tx_battery_bars:
        type: integer
        label: Battery Bars
        min: 0
        max: 6
        help: "Battery bars as the transmitter's display shows them."
      tx_battery_health_percent:
        type: integer
        label: Battery Health
        min: 0
        max: 100
        unit: "%"
        help: "The docked transmitter's battery health; 0 when the bay is empty."
      tx_battery_cycles:
        type: integer
        label: Battery Cycles
        help: "Charging cycles of the docked transmitter's battery."
      identifying:
        type: boolean
        label: Identifying
        help: "The bay's LEDs are flashing to show which bay it is (for 10 seconds)."
      status:
        type: enum
        values: [normal, updating, error]
        label: Bay Status
        cloud_priority: high
        help: "normal, updating (the docked transmitter's firmware is updating), or error (see the four error flags)."
      communication_error:
        type: boolean
        label: Communication Error
        cloud_priority: high
        help: "The charger cannot talk to the transmitter in this bay."
      update_error:
        type: boolean
        label: Update Error
        cloud_priority: high
        help: "Updating the docked transmitter's firmware failed."
      overcurrent:
        type: boolean
        label: Overcurrent
        cloud_priority: high
        help: "The bay detected an overcurrent."
      no_charging_voltage:
        type: boolean
        label: No Charging Voltage
        cloud_priority: high
        help: "The bay's 5 V charging voltage is missing."

commands:
  identify:
    label: Identify Bay
    help: >
      Flashes the LEDs of the chosen bay, or every bay, for 10 seconds so it
      can be found on the charger. Stop identifying ends it sooner.
    send: '{"bays":{"identify":[{bay}]}}'
    params:
      bay:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: Bay
        options_state: identify_options
        # One true, false or null per bay, two or four of them (§14.53).
        pattern: '^(?:true|false|null)(?:,(?:true|false|null)|(?:,(?:true|false|null)){3})$'
        help: "Pick a bay. The choices appear once the charger has connected and reported its model."
  restart:
    label: Restart Charger
    help: "Restarts the charger. It is off the network until it is back."
    send: '{"device":{"reset":true}}'
    confirm: "Restarts the charger. It is off the network until it is back."
    # The document gives no boot time; not yet measured on a unit.
    restarts_device_for: 90
  factory_reset:
    label: Factory Reset
    help: "Returns every setting on the charger to its factory default and restarts it."
    send: '{"device":{"factory_reset":true}}'
    confirm: "Returns every setting on the charger to its factory default, its name and network settings included, and restarts it."
    restarts_device_for: 90

quick_actions: [identify]

actions:
  - id: identify
    icon: sun

device_settings:
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: Device Name
    help: "The charger's name in Control Cockpit and in discovery. No double quotes or backslashes."
    state_key: device_name
    default: "CHG4N"
    regex: '^[^"\\]{1,64}$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"name":"{value}"}}'
  group:
    type: string
    label: Group
    help: "Up to 8 letters, digits, - and _, starting with a letter and ending with a letter or digit."
    state_key: group
    default: ""
    regex: '^(?:[A-Za-z](?:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,6}[A-Za-z0-9])?)?$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"group":"{value}"}}'
  location:
    type: string
    label: Location
    help: "Where the charger is. No double quotes or backslashes."
    state_key: location
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"\\]{0,64}$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"location":"{value}"}}'
  mdns_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: mDNS
    help: "The charger announces itself for discovery. Takes effect after the charger restarts."
    state_key: mdns_enabled
    default: true
    map: { "true": "true", "false": "false" }
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"network":{"mdns_responder":{value}}}}'

responses:
  # ── Every value the charger reports about itself ──
  # Each answer and notification is an address tree; a body without a key
  # leaves that key's variable alone.
  - json: true
    set:
      model: device.identity.product
      bay_count_reported:
        key: device.identity.product
        map: { "CHG2N": 2, "CHG4N": 4 }
      # Identify Bay's choices: each is the model's own identify array (one
      # element per bay, null leaving a bay as it is).
      identify_options:
        key: device.identity.product
        map:
          "CHG2N": '[{"value":"true,null","label":"Bay 1"},{"value":"null,true","label":"Bay 2"},{"value":"true,true","label":"All bays"},{"value":"false,false","label":"Stop identifying"}]'
          "CHG4N": '[{"value":"true,null,null,null","label":"Bay 1"},{"value":"null,true,null,null","label":"Bay 2"},{"value":"null,null,true,null","label":"Bay 3"},{"value":"null,null,null,true","label":"Bay 4"},{"value":"true,true,true,true","label":"All bays"},{"value":"false,false,false,false","label":"Stop identifying"}]'
      firmware_version: device.identity.version
      serial_number: device.identity.serial
      vendor: device.identity.vendor
      interface_version: interface.version
      mac_address: device.network.ether.macs.0
      ip_address: device.network.ipv4.ipaddr.0
      mdns_enabled: device.network.mdns_responder
      device_name: device.name
      group: device.group
      location: device.location
      device_state:
        key: device.state
        map: { "0": normal, "1": firmware_update }
      progress: device.progress
      sl_firmware_image: device.ptxversion_sl
      d1_firmware_image: device.ptxversion_d1

  # ── Every bay value: element n of each array is bay n+1 ──
  # Bays 1 and 2 here; bays 3 and 4 in the rule after it, which stops reading
  # once the charger has reported two bays (a CHG 2N has neither, and its
  # roster drops them). Until the model is reported, all four are read.
  # /bays/state is two arrays: the bay's state, then its errors as bits
  # (§14.54).
  - json: true
    child_set:
      - type: bay
        id: 1
        state:
          docked: bays.active.0
          tx_type: { key: bays.device_type.0, map: &tx_types { "0": null, "1": handheld, "2": bodypack } }
          tx_serial: bays.serial.0
          tx_firmware: bays.version.0
          tx_charging: bays.charging.0
          tx_battery_percent: bays.bat_gauge.0
          tx_charge_minutes: bays.bat_timetofull.0
          tx_battery_bars: bays.bat_bars.0
          tx_battery_health_percent: bays.bat_health.0
          tx_battery_cycles: bays.bat_cycles.0
          identifying: bays.identify.0
          status: { key: bays.state.0.0, map: &bay_states { "0": normal, "1": updating, "2": error } }
          # Bit 0 communication, bit 1 update, bit 2 overcurrent, bit 3 the 5 V
          # charging voltage: one map per bit over every 4-bit value.
          communication_error: { key: bays.state.1.0, map: &bit0 { "0": false, "1": true, "2": false, "3": true, "4": false, "5": true, "6": false, "7": true, "8": false, "9": true, "10": false, "11": true, "12": false, "13": true, "14": false, "15": true } }
          update_error: { key: bays.state.1.0, map: &bit1 { "0": false, "1": false, "2": true, "3": true, "4": false, "5": false, "6": true, "7": true, "8": false, "9": false, "10": true, "11": true, "12": false, "13": false, "14": true, "15": true } }
          overcurrent: { key: bays.state.1.0, map: &bit2 { "0": false, "1": false, "2": false, "3": false, "4": true, "5": true, "6": true, "7": true, "8": false, "9": false, "10": false, "11": false, "12": true, "13": true, "14": true, "15": true } }
          no_charging_voltage: { key: bays.state.1.0, map: &bit3 { "0": false, "1": false, "2": false, "3": false, "4": false, "5": false, "6": false, "7": false, "8": true, "9": true, "10": true, "11": true, "12": true, "13": true, "14": true, "15": true } }
      - type: bay
        id: 2
        state:
          docked: bays.active.1
          tx_type: { key: bays.device_type.1, map: *tx_types }
          tx_serial: bays.serial.1
          tx_firmware: bays.version.1
          tx_charging: bays.charging.1
          tx_battery_percent: bays.bat_gauge.1
          tx_charge_minutes: bays.bat_timetofull.1
          tx_battery_bars: bays.bat_bars.1
          tx_battery_health_percent: bays.bat_health.1
          tx_battery_cycles: bays.bat_cycles.1
          identifying: bays.identify.1
          status: { key: bays.state.0.1, map: *bay_states }
          communication_error: { key: bays.state.1.1, map: *bit0 }
          update_error: { key: bays.state.1.1, map: *bit1 }
          overcurrent: { key: bays.state.1.1, map: *bit2 }
          no_charging_voltage: { key: bays.state.1.1, map: *bit3 }
  - json: true
    only_when: { any: [{ key: bay_count_reported, value: 4 }, { key: bay_count_reported, operator: falsy }] }
    child_set:
      - type: bay
        id: 3
        state:
          docked: bays.active.2
          tx_type: { key: bays.device_type.2, map: *tx_types }
          tx_serial: bays.serial.2
          tx_firmware: bays.version.2
          tx_charging: bays.charging.2
          tx_battery_percent: bays.bat_gauge.2
          tx_charge_minutes: bays.bat_timetofull.2
          tx_battery_bars: bays.bat_bars.2
          tx_battery_health_percent: bays.bat_health.2
          tx_battery_cycles: bays.bat_cycles.2
          identifying: bays.identify.2
          status: { key: bays.state.0.2, map: *bay_states }
          communication_error: { key: bays.state.1.2, map: *bit0 }
          update_error: { key: bays.state.1.2, map: *bit1 }
          overcurrent: { key: bays.state.1.2, map: *bit2 }
          no_charging_voltage: { key: bays.state.1.2, map: *bit3 }
      - type: bay
        id: 4
        state:
          docked: bays.active.3
          tx_type: { key: bays.device_type.3, map: *tx_types }
          tx_serial: bays.serial.3
          tx_firmware: bays.version.3
          tx_charging: bays.charging.3
          tx_battery_percent: bays.bat_gauge.3
          tx_charge_minutes: bays.bat_timetofull.3
          tx_battery_bars: bays.bat_bars.3
          tx_battery_health_percent: bays.bat_health.3
          tx_battery_cycles: bays.bat_cycles.3
          identifying: bays.identify.3
          status: { key: bays.state.0.3, map: *bay_states }
          communication_error: { key: bays.state.1.3, map: *bit0 }
          update_error: { key: bays.state.1.3, map: *bit1 }
          overcurrent: { key: bays.state.1.3, map: *bit2 }
          no_charging_voltage: { key: bays.state.1.3, map: *bit3 }

  # Every rule below reads text, and each may meet a reply the json rules
  # above also read (a subscription's answer can carry its current value), so
  # every one stays eligible past them (after_json). The first that matches
  # wins.

  # ── A subscription ended (310, §5.1): subscribe everything again ──
  # The poll would renew it within 30 s; this does it at once. Reading the
  # text also catches a 310 that is not valid JSON, as the document's own
  # multi-address example is not.
  - match: '"error"\s*:.*?\[\s*310\b'
    after_json: true
    set: {}
    then_query:
      - *sub_name
      - *sub_group
      - *sub_location
      - *sub_mdns
      - *sub_state
      - *sub_progress
      - *sub_sl_image
      - *sub_d1_image
      - *sub_active
      - *sub_serial
      - *sub_version
      - *sub_charging
      - *sub_gauge
      - *sub_timetofull
      - *sub_bars
      - *sub_health
      - *sub_cycles
      - *sub_identify

  # ── A refused read or subscription of the serial numbers ──
  # They need a transmitter in a bay (§14.44). The driver never writes them,
  # so a refusal answers a subscription sent as the last transmitter left
  # (or one the driver last saw docked before a reconnect) and is not an
  # error to show.
  - match: '"error"\s*:.*?"serial"\s*:\s*\[\s*\d{3}'
    after_json: true
    set: {}

  # ── Any other refusal (§14.4, §15) ──
  # {"osc":{"error":[{"bays":{"identify":[406]}}]}}, or [400] for a message
  # the charger could not read; a "desc" may follow the code.
  - match: '"error"\s*:.*?\[\s*(\d{3})\b'
    after_json: true
    mappings:
      - { group: 1, state: last_error_code, type: integer }
      - group: 1
        state: last_error
        map:
          "400": "The charger could not read the request (400)."
          "403": "The charger refused the request (403)."
          "404": "The charger has no such setting (404)."
          "406": "The charger did not accept the value, or cannot change it now (406)."
          "409": "The request conflicts with the charger's current state (409)."
          "413": "The request was too large for the charger (413)."
          "414": "The request was too complex for the charger (414)."
          "422": "The charger could not carry out the request (422)."
          "423": "The setting is locked on the charger (423)."
          "450": "The charger's answer would be too long (450)."
          "454": "The charger keeps that setting hidden (454)."
          "500": "The charger had an internal error (500)."
          "501": "The charger does not support that request (501)."
          "503": "The charger is busy (503)."

  # ── The docked bays (/bays/active, §14.42) ──
  # Each bay's transmitter type and error state cannot be subscribed, so
  # they are read again whenever the docked bays are reported (the poll
  # reads them too, on releases without then_query). The first transmitter
  # docked also subscribes the serial numbers.
  - match: '"bays"\s*:\s*\{\s*"active"\s*:\s*\[[^\]]*\btrue\b'
    after_json: true
    only_when: { key: transmitters_docked, operator: falsy }
    set: { transmitters_docked: "true" }
    then_query:
      - *sub_serial
      - *read_types
      - *read_bay_state
  - match: '"bays"\s*:\s*\{\s*"active"\s*:\s*\[[^\]]*\btrue\b'
    after_json: true
    set: { transmitters_docked: "true" }
    then_query:
      - *read_types
      - *read_bay_state
  # Every bay empty. The serial numbers are no longer subscribed, so a
  # transmitter that left while the driver was away would keep its number:
  # clear them, as the charger itself reports an empty bay: two bays on a
  # charger that has reported two, else four.
  - match: '"bays"\s*:\s*\{\s*"active"\s*:\s*\['
    after_json: true
    only_when: { any: [{ key: bay_count_reported, value: 4 }, { key: bay_count_reported, operator: falsy }] }
    set: { transmitters_docked: "false" }
    child_set:
      - { type: bay, id: 1, state: { tx_serial: "" } }
      - { type: bay, id: 2, state: { tx_serial: "" } }
      - { type: bay, id: 3, state: { tx_serial: "" } }
      - { type: bay, id: 4, state: { tx_serial: "" } }
    then_query:
      - *read_types
      - *read_bay_state
  - match: '"bays"\s*:\s*\{\s*"active"\s*:\s*\['
    after_json: true
    set: { transmitters_docked: "false" }
    child_set:
      - { type: bay, id: 1, state: { tx_serial: "" } }
      - { type: bay, id: 2, state: { tx_serial: "" } }
    then_query:
      - *read_types
      - *read_bay_state

  # ── Restart and Factory Reset are answered with themselves ──
  - match: '"device"\s*:\s*\{\s*"(?:reset|factory_reset)"\s*:\s*true'
    after_json: true
    set: {}

  # ── A subscription's own answer ── carries nothing the rules above have not
  # read; acknowledged here so it does not count as a reply nobody read.
  - match: '"osc"\s*:\s*\{\s*"state"\s*:\s*\{\s*"subscribe"'
    after_json: true
    set: {}

# ── SIMULATOR ──
# One script handler is the whole SSC server: it parses the incoming JSON
# object, walks the address tree against the method table below, answers
# every address with its value, records subscriptions and answers each with
# the current value bundled after the echo, and refuses what the document
# says the charger refuses (404 for an unknown address or a subscription to
# an address that cannot be subscribed, 406 for a write to a read-only
# address, an identify array of the wrong length, or the serial numbers with
# every bay empty).
#
# The model follows the device's Charging Bays setting: 2 answers as a CHG
# 2N, anything else as a CHG 4N. Each bay's values live in bayN_* keys; a bay
# with no transmitter answers false, 0 or "" whatever its keys hold, as the
# charger reports an empty bay. Flags are the words "true" and "false", so
# they go into a notification as JSON.
#
# The Simulator UI's bay controls send the whole array for that value as
# notifications: through the notifications: map below. Those always carry four
# elements, so a simulated CHG 2N pushes two more than it has (the driver
# reads its own two); every answer to a read or a subscription has the
# model's own length. Docking or emptying a bay pushes the docked bays only:
# its battery and other values follow at the next renewal.
#
# Not modelled (the sandbox has no clock): a subscription's lifetime and its
# 1000-notification limit (the End Subscriptions control sends the 310 the
# charger would), identify's 10 seconds, a firmware update, and the restart
# after Restart or Factory Reset. Notifications go out whether or not the
# address is subscribed.
simulator:
  initial_state:
    _subscriptions: ""
    end_subscriptions: false
    firmware_version: "3.0.0"
    serial_number: "1454100930"
    vendor: "Sennheiser electronic GmbH & Co. KG"
    interface_version: "1.0"
    mac_address: "00:1B:66:7D:F8:99"
    ip_address: "192.168.1.203"
    mdns_enabled: true
    device_name: "CHG4N"
    group: "room"
    location: "Meeting Room A"
    device_state: "normal"
    progress: 0
    sl_firmware_image: "0.7.4"
    d1_firmware_image: "0.7.4"
    # Bay 1 empty, bay 2 a full handheld, bays 3 and 4 charging.
    bay1_docked: "false"
    bay1_type: "none"
    bay1_serial: ""
    bay1_version: ""
    bay1_linkdate: 0
    bay1_charging: "false"
    bay1_battery: 0
    bay1_minutes: 0
    bay1_bars: 0
    bay1_health: 0
    bay1_cycles: 0
    bay1_identify: "false"
    bay1_errors: 0
    bay2_docked: "true"
    bay2_type: "handheld"
    bay2_serial: "1106103018"
    bay2_version: "0.7.3"
    bay2_linkdate: 1606021157
    bay2_charging: "false"
    bay2_battery: 100
    bay2_minutes: 0
    bay2_bars: 6
    bay2_health: 95
    bay2_cycles: 20
    bay2_identify: "false"
    bay2_errors: 0
    bay3_docked: "true"
    bay3_type: "bodypack"
    bay3_serial: "1106103029"
    bay3_version: "0.7.4"
    bay3_linkdate: 1605201510
    bay3_charging: "true"
    bay3_battery: 64
    bay3_minutes: 85
    bay3_bars: 4
    bay3_health: 100
    bay3_cycles: 28
    bay3_identify: "false"
    bay3_errors: 0
    bay4_docked: "true"
    bay4_type: "handheld"
    bay4_serial: "1106103023"
    bay4_version: "0.7.3"
    bay4_linkdate: 1605101917
    bay4_charging: "true"
    bay4_battery: 30
    bay4_minutes: 100
    bay4_bars: 2
    bay4_health: 100
    bay4_cycles: 16
    bay4_identify: "false"
    bay4_errors: 0

  delays:
    command_response: 0.02

  controls:
    - { type: select, key: device_state, label: Charger State, options: [normal, firmware_update] }
    - { type: slider, key: progress, label: Update Progress (%), min: 0, max: 100 }
    - { type: select, key: bay1_docked, label: Bay 1 Transmitter Docked, options: ["true", "false"] }
    - { type: slider, key: bay1_battery, label: Bay 1 Battery (%), min: 0, max: 100 }
    - { type: select, key: bay1_charging, label: Bay 1 Charging, options: ["true", "false"] }
    - { type: slider, key: bay1_errors, label: Bay 1 Error Bits, min: 0, max: 15 }
    - { type: select, key: bay2_docked, label: Bay 2 Transmitter Docked, options: ["true", "false"] }
    - { type: slider, key: bay2_battery, label: Bay 2 Battery (%), min: 0, max: 100 }
    - { type: select, key: bay2_charging, label: Bay 2 Charging, options: ["true", "false"] }
    - { type: slider, key: bay2_errors, label: Bay 2 Error Bits, min: 0, max: 15 }
    - { type: select, key: bay3_docked, label: Bay 3 Transmitter Docked, options: ["true", "false"] }
    - { type: slider, key: bay3_battery, label: Bay 3 Battery (%), min: 0, max: 100 }
    - { type: select, key: bay3_charging, label: Bay 3 Charging, options: ["true", "false"] }
    - { type: slider, key: bay3_errors, label: Bay 3 Error Bits, min: 0, max: 15 }
    - { type: select, key: bay4_docked, label: Bay 4 Transmitter Docked, options: ["true", "false"] }
    - { type: slider, key: bay4_battery, label: Bay 4 Battery (%), min: 0, max: 100 }
    - { type: select, key: bay4_charging, label: Bay 4 Charging, options: ["true", "false"] }
    - { type: slider, key: bay4_errors, label: Bay 4 Error Bits, min: 0, max: 15 }
    - { type: toggle, key: end_subscriptions, label: End Subscriptions (310) }

  # What the charger sends, unasked, when a value changes. A bay value goes
  # out as its whole array.
  notifications:
    device_name: '{"device":{"name":"{value}"}}'
    group: '{"device":{"group":"{value}"}}'
    location: '{"device":{"location":"{value}"}}'
    mdns_enabled:
      'true': '{"device":{"network":{"mdns_responder":true}}}'
      'false': '{"device":{"network":{"mdns_responder":false}}}'
    device_state:
      normal: '{"device":{"state":0}}'
      firmware_update: '{"device":{"state":1}}'
    progress: '{"device":{"progress":{value}}}'
    bay1_docked: &push_active '{"bays":{"active":[{state.bay1_docked},{state.bay2_docked},{state.bay3_docked},{state.bay4_docked}]}}'
    bay2_docked: *push_active
    bay3_docked: *push_active
    bay4_docked: *push_active
    bay1_battery: &push_gauge '{"bays":{"bat_gauge":[{state.bay1_battery},{state.bay2_battery},{state.bay3_battery},{state.bay4_battery}]}}'
    bay2_battery: *push_gauge
    bay3_battery: *push_gauge
    bay4_battery: *push_gauge
    bay1_charging: &push_charging '{"bays":{"charging":[{state.bay1_charging},{state.bay2_charging},{state.bay3_charging},{state.bay4_charging}]}}'
    bay2_charging: *push_charging
    bay3_charging: *push_charging
    bay4_charging: *push_charging
    # The charger's end of a subscription (§5.1), on demand.
    end_subscriptions:
      'true': '{"osc":{"error":[{"bays":{"active":[310]}}]}}'

  command_handlers:
    # Everything the socket receives goes through the one SSC server, so a
    # message that is not JSON gets the document's 400, not silence.
    - match: '(?s:.*)'
      handler: |
        def _run():
            text = match.group(0)

            # A whole float prints as an integer, as the charger writes it.
            def plain(v):
                if v.__class__ is float and v == int(v):
                    return int(v)
                if v.__class__ is dict:
                    return {k: plain(x) for k, x in v.items()}
                if v.__class__ is list:
                    return [plain(x) for x in v]
                return v

            def dumps(v):
                return json.dumps(plain(v), separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False)

            count = 2 if str(config.get("bay_count") or "4").strip() == "2" else 4
            product = "CHG2N" if count == 2 else "CHG4N"
            BAYS = [1, 2, 3, 4][:count]
            TYPES = ["none", "handheld", "bodypack"]
            STATES = ["normal", "firmware_update"]

            def word(v):
                return v is True or str(v).strip().lower() == "true"

            def bay(n, key):
                return state["bay%d_%s" % (n, key)]

            def docked(n):
                return word(bay(n, "docked"))

            def any_docked():
                for n in BAYS:
                    if docked(n):
                        return True
                return False

            # dotted address -> (kind, state key, extra, pre-condition, subscribable)
            # Charger kinds: ro (read only), product, list1 (a one-element
            # list), bool, str, idx (words: the charger's number is the
            # index), fixed (a constant), trigger (write only). Bay kinds
            # answer one element per bay: bay_bool, bay_int, bay_str,
            # bay_type, bay_state (two arrays), identify (writable).
            LEAVES = {
                "interface.version": ("ro", "interface_version", None, None, False),
                "device.identity.product": ("product", None, None, None, False),
                "device.identity.version": ("ro", "firmware_version", None, None, False),
                "device.identity.serial": ("ro", "serial_number", None, None, False),
                "device.identity.vendor": ("ro", "vendor", None, None, False),
                "device.network.ether.interfaces": ("fixed", None, ["LAN"], None, False),
                "device.network.ether.macs": ("list1", "mac_address", None, None, False),
                "device.network.ipv4.ipaddr": ("list1", "ip_address", None, None, False),
                "device.network.mdns_responder": ("bool", "mdns_enabled", None, None, True),
                "device.name": ("str", "device_name", None, None, True),
                "device.group": ("str", "group", None, None, True),
                "device.location": ("str", "location", None, None, True),
                "device.language": ("fixed", None, ["en_GB"], None, False),
                "device.state": ("idx", "device_state", STATES, None, True),
                "device.progress": ("ro", "progress", None, None, True),
                "device.ptxversion_sl": ("ro", "sl_firmware_image", None, None, True),
                "device.ptxversion_d1": ("ro", "d1_firmware_image", None, None, True),
                "device.warnings": ("fixed", None, [""], None, False),
                "device.reset": ("trigger", None, None, None, False),
                "device.factory_reset": ("trigger", None, None, None, False),
                "bays.active": ("bay_bool", "docked", None, None, True),
                "bays.device_type": ("bay_type", "type", None, None, False),
                "bays.serial": ("bay_str", "serial", None, "docked", True),
                "bays.version": ("bay_str", "version", None, None, True),
                "bays.linkdate": ("bay_int", "linkdate", None, None, True),
                "bays.charging": ("bay_bool", "charging", None, None, True),
                "bays.bat_gauge": ("bay_int", "battery", None, None, True),
                "bays.bat_timetofull": ("bay_int", "minutes", None, None, True),
                "bays.bat_bars": ("bay_int", "bars", None, None, True),
                "bays.bat_health": ("bay_int", "health", None, None, True),
                "bays.bat_cycles": ("bay_int", "cycles", None, None, True),
                "bays.identify": ("identify", "identify", None, None, True),
                "bays.state": ("bay_state", "errors", None, None, False),
            }
            OSC = {
                "osc.version": "1.0",
                "osc.feature.pattern": "*?",
                "osc.feature.baseaddr": False,
                "osc.feature.subscription": True,
                "osc.feature.timetag": False,
                "osc.state.prettyprint": False,
            }

            def holds(pre):
                if pre == "docked":
                    return any_docked()
                return True

            def element(n, kind, key):
                # An empty bay reports false, 0 or "" whatever its keys hold.
                if kind == "identify":
                    return word(bay(n, key))
                if kind == "bay_bool":
                    return docked(n) and word(bay(n, key))
                if not docked(n):
                    return "" if kind == "bay_str" else 0
                if kind == "bay_int":
                    return int(bay(n, key))
                if kind == "bay_str":
                    return str(bay(n, key))
                if kind == "bay_type":
                    t = bay(n, key)
                    return TYPES.index(t) if t in TYPES else 0
                return None

            def current(spec):
                kind, key, extra = spec[0], spec[1], spec[2]
                if kind == "product":
                    return product
                if kind == "fixed":
                    return extra
                if kind == "idx":
                    w = state[key]
                    return extra.index(w) if w in extra else 0
                if kind == "list1":
                    return [state[key]]
                if kind == "bool":
                    return word(state[key])
                if kind == "bay_state":
                    errors = [int(bay(n, key)) if docked(n) else 0 for n in BAYS]
                    return [[2 if e else 0 for e in errors], errors]
                if kind in ("bay_bool", "bay_int", "bay_str", "bay_type", "identify"):
                    return [element(n, kind, key) for n in BAYS]
                if kind == "trigger":
                    return None
                return state[key]

            # A refused address is reported under osc.error and left out of
            # the answer; NO marks it.
            NO = ("refused",)

            def apply(spec, value):
                # (result, error code)
                kind, key = spec[0], spec[1]
                if kind == "bool":
                    if value.__class__ is not bool:
                        return NO, 406
                    state[key] = value
                    return value, 0
                if kind == "str":
                    if value.__class__ is not str:
                        return NO, 406
                    state[key] = value
                    return value, 0
                if kind == "trigger":
                    if value is not True:
                        return NO, 406
                    return True, 0
                if kind == "identify":
                    if value.__class__ is not list or len(value) != count:
                        return NO, 406
                    for v in value:
                        if v is not None and v.__class__ is not bool:
                            return NO, 406
                    i = 0
                    for n in BAYS:
                        if value[i] is not None:
                            state["bay%d_identify" % n] = "true" if value[i] else "false"
                        i += 1
                    return current(spec), 0
                return NO, 406

            members = []
            errors = []

            def tree(path, value):
                node = value
                for seg in path[::-1]:
                    node = {seg: node}
                return node

            def member(path, value):
                members.append(dumps(tree(path, value))[1:-1])

            def fail(path, code):
                errors.append(tree(path, [code]))

            def leaves_of(node, prefix):
                out = []
                for key, val in node.items():
                    if key == "#":
                        continue
                    path = prefix + [key]
                    dotted = ".".join(path)
                    if val.__class__ is dict and dotted not in LEAVES:
                        out.extend(leaves_of(val, path))
                    else:
                        out.append((path, val))
                return out

            def subscriptions():
                return [p for p in state["_subscriptions"].split(",") if p]

            def subscribe(value):
                if value is None:
                    tr = {}
                    for p in subscriptions():
                        node = tr
                        segs = p.split(".")
                        for seg in segs[:-1]:
                            node = node.setdefault(seg, {})
                        node[segs[-1]] = None
                    member(["osc", "state", "subscribe"], [tr])
                    return
                if value.__class__ is not list:
                    value = [value]
                subs = subscriptions()
                echoed = []
                initial = []
                for entry in value:
                    if entry.__class__ is not dict:
                        continue
                    params = entry.get("#")
                    cancel = params.__class__ is dict and params.get("cancel") is True
                    good = []
                    for path, _val in leaves_of(entry, []):
                        dotted = ".".join(path)
                        spec = LEAVES.get(dotted)
                        if spec is None or not spec[4]:
                            fail(["osc", "state", "subscribe"] + path, 404)
                            continue
                        if not cancel and not holds(spec[3]):
                            fail(path, 406)
                            continue
                        good.append(path)
                        if cancel:
                            subs = [p for p in subs if p != dotted]
                        else:
                            if dotted not in subs:
                                subs.append(dotted)
                            initial.append((path, current(spec)))
                    if not good:
                        continue
                    # The echo of an entry, one member per address.
                    parts = []
                    if params.__class__ is dict:
                        parts.append(dumps({"#": params})[1:-1])
                    for path in good:
                        parts.append(dumps(tree(path, None))[1:-1])
                    echoed.append("{" + ",".join(parts) + "}")
                state["_subscriptions"] = ",".join(subs)
                if echoed:
                    members.append('"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[' + ",".join(echoed) + "]}}")
                for path, val in initial:
                    member(path, val)

            def handle(path, value):
                dotted = ".".join(path)
                if dotted == "osc.xid":
                    member(path, value)
                elif dotted == "osc.state.subscribe":
                    subscribe(value)
                elif dotted == "osc.state.close":
                    state["_subscriptions"] = ""
                    member(path, True)
                elif dotted in OSC:
                    if value is not None:
                        fail(path, 406)
                    else:
                        member(path, OSC[dotted])
                elif dotted in LEAVES:
                    spec = LEAVES[dotted]
                    if not holds(spec[3]):
                        fail(path, 406)
                    elif value is None:
                        if spec[0] == "trigger":
                            fail(path, 406)
                        else:
                            member(path, current(spec))
                    else:
                        result, code = apply(spec, value)
                        if result is NO:
                            fail(path, code)
                        else:
                            member(path, result)
                else:
                    fail(path, 404)

            try:
                request = json.loads(text)
                if request.__class__ is not dict:
                    raise ValueError("not an object")
            except ValueError:
                respond('{"osc":{"error":[400]}}')
                return

            for path, value in leaves_of(request, []):
                handle(path, value)
            if errors:
                members.append(dumps({"osc": {"error": errors}})[1:-1])
            respond("{" + ",".join(members) + "}")

        _run()
